# November 23, 2026: Leavenworth County, Kansas (Leavenworth and the country round it). The Atlas had nothing here.
# Fifteen places from the National Register list for the county: the railroad depots, the 1913 courthouse, the Carnegie
# library, an Art Deco theatre, a church with Tiffany glass, two houses, the Soldiers' Home, a factory, a church in the
# fields, a truss bridge and a one-room school.
# Facts from the linked sources only: National Register forms read in full text, Wikipedia read one article at a time,
# the Kansas Historical Society's register search and the pages of the bodies that run the places.
